The data come from Atmo Data (https://admindata.atmo-france.org), produced by
the regional air quality monitoring associations (AASQA) and aggregated by the
Fédération Atmo France, under the Open Database License (ODbL). Each reading
shows its source AASQA, as the licence requires. Communes are found with
geo.api.gouv.fr, an open API of the French government.

The way the Atmo Data API is read was learned from the Home Assistant
integration atmofrance by sebcaps (MIT, https://github.com/sebcaps/atmofrance)
and from the Recosante project of the French government (Apache 2.0,
https://github.com/SocialGouv/recosante). No file of either is included.

This community integration is not affiliated with, endorsed or sponsored by
the Fédération Atmo France or the AASQA.
